---
import Layout from '../../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../../../../styles/equipment.css';
import checks from '../../../../../public/equipment/13-12/verification.json';
import m from '../../../../../public/equipment/13-12/interactions.json';
import {labels,AUTHOR_ID} from '../../../../lib/equipment/13-12/solver.mjs';
const a='/equipment/13-12/',photo='https://bioem.ucdavis.edu/pelco-easiglow-glow-discharge-system',spec='https://www.tedpella.com/easiGlow_html/Glow-Discharge-Cleaning-System.aspx';
const display=x=>Object.entries(x??{}).map(([k,v])=>k+': '+String(v)).join('; ');
---
<Layout pageTitle="PELCO easiGlow 91000 documentary exterior" subtitle="" description="Inspect a fixed easiGlow enclosure and add notes to two separate inert drawings." wide={true}>
<article id="eg" class="equipment"><nav class="eq-nav"><a href="/simulations/equipment/13-12/">← Equipment 13-12</a><a href="/simulations/equipment/">Equipment register</a><a href="#eg-checks">Verification</a></nav>
<header><p class="eq-meta">13-12 / PELCO easiGlow 91000 / Static exterior and inert documentation</p><h2>PELCO easiGlow 91000</h2><p>Inspect the unpowered standalone enclosure, then add review tags to two independent drawing cards on the separate desk. A note on card A leaves card B unchanged, and neither note alters either card’s geometry.</p></header>
<div class="e-grid"><section class="e-card"><h3>01 · Inspect the closed model</h3><div id="eg-views" class="e-row">{['Bench','Front','Exterior','Desk'].map(k=><button type="button" data-view={k.toLowerCase()}>{k}</button>)}<button id="eg-xr" type="button" disabled>VR unavailable</button></div><canvas id="eg-model" aria-label="Orbitable static PELCO easiGlow enclosure and separate drawing cards"></canvas><p id="eg-asset" role="status">Loading metric GLB…</p><p class="e-hint">Click either colored card to select it and the brass desk button to add a tag. The equipment panel and tinted bell are fixed, with no functional controls. Drag to orbit, scroll or pinch to zoom.</p></section>
<section class="e-card"><h3>02 · Add an inert drawing tag</h3><form id="eg-form"><div class="e-fields"><label>Card<select id="eg-card"><option value="A">A · Notched outline</option><option value="B">B · Crosshair</option></select></label><label>Review label<select id="eg-label">{Object.entries(labels).map(([k,v])=><option value={k}>{v}</option>)}</select></label></div><div class="e-row"><button id="eg-add" class="e-run" type="submit">Add review tag</button><button id="eg-example" type="button">Load example on A</button><button id="eg-reset" type="button">Clear tags</button></div></form><p id="eg-status" role="status">Card A selected · revision 0.</p><p>All tags use the fixed demo author <code>{AUTHOR_ID}</code>. This is synthetic provenance, not a claim about who used an instrument.</p></section></div>
<section class="e-card"><h3>03 · Review both drawing records</h3><div class="e-grid">{[['A','Notched outline'],['B','Crosshair']].map(([k,n])=><section class="drawing-card" id={'eg-info-'+k}><h4>Card {k} · {n}</h4><p>42 × 28 mm · geometry is immutable.</p><button id={'eg-pick-'+k} type="button">Select {k}</button><ul id={'eg-notes-'+k}><li>No annotations.</li></ul></section>)}</div><div class="e-row"><button id="eg-json" disabled>Drawing review JSON</button></div><p>The export preserves both source IDs, fixed author, note ordering, dimensions, vertex coordinates and triangle indices. This is annotation on an original representation, not a physical grid or state. <a href={a+'example-review.json'}>Example JSON</a>.</p></section>
<section><h3>Reference geometry</h3><div class="e-grid"><figure><img src={a+'original-front.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original metric easiGlow exterior and two independent cards"/><figcaption>Original standalone 91000 exterior informed by the <a href={photo}>UC Davis reference photograph</a>. The annotation desk is original, separate, and not an accessory.</figcaption></figure><figure><img src={a+'original-work.svg'} width="760" height="450" alt="Original representation of the fixed bell and blank angled panel"/><figcaption>Fixed bell and blank display silhouette. No working parts are modeled.</figcaption></figure></div>
<p>The <a href={spec}>manufacturer’s 91000 specification</a> lists 305 × 292 × 230 mm for the standalone envelope and Ø120 × 100 mm for the exterior bell. Panel details, shape transitions and foot geometry are inferred. No other equipment is connected. The register’s physical treatment-state acceptance is out of scope; only independent documentation records are tested.</p></section>
<section id="eg-checks"><h3>Verification and files</h3><div class="e-over"><table><thead><tr><th>Case</th><th>Expected</th><th>Actual</th><th>Status</th></tr></thead><tbody>{checks.map(x=><tr><td>{x.id}</td><td>{display(x.expected)}</td><td>{display(x.actual)}</td><td>{x.pass?'Pass':'Fail'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div>
<p><a href={a+'reference-plan.json'}>Predeclared cases</a> · <a href={a+'verification.json'}>Verification data</a> · <a href={a+'pelco-easiglow-91000.glb'} download>Metric GLB</a> · <a href={a+'geometry-source.mjs'}>Editable geometry</a> + <a href={a+'make-model.mjs'}>generator</a> + <a href={a+'mesh-writer.mjs'}>mesh writer</a> · <a href={a+'interactions.json'}>Named targets</a>. {m.triangles.toLocaleString()} triangles and {m.draws} draw primitives; optional WebXR, physical headset untested.</p></section></article></Layout>
<script>import '../../../../lib/equipment/13-12/client.mjs';</script>
<style>
#eg header{max-width:73ch;padding:1.3rem 0}#eg h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,6vw,4rem);margin:.2rem 0}#eg section{margin:1rem 0}.e-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.e-card{border:1px solid var(--border);padding:.8rem;min-width:0}.e-card h3{margin:.3rem 0}.e-row{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.4rem;margin:.5rem 0}.e-fields{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.55rem}.e-fields label{display:grid;gap:.2rem}.e-fields input,#eg button{min-width:0;min-height:2.45rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:3px;background:var(--panel);color:var(--text);font:inherit;padding:.3rem .5rem;box-sizing:border-box}#eg button:disabled{opacity:.52}.e-run{background:#3d596e!important;color:white!important}#eg-model{width:100%;height:clamp(280px,34vw,440px);display:block;background:#ebe8e0;touch-action:none}#eg-chart{width:100%;max-height:16rem}.e-over{overflow:auto}#eg table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:.85rem}#eg td,#eg th{text-align:left;padding:.45rem;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border)}#eg figure{margin:0}#eg img{width:100%;height:auto}@media(max-width:820px){.e-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.e-fields{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr))}}
#eg caption{text-align:left}#eg input,#eg select,#eg button{min-width:0}#eg .e-hint{font-size:.92rem}#eg .selected{border-color:#b38a58}#eg .drawing-card{padding:1rem;border:1px solid var(--border);min-width:0}#eg .drawing-card h4{margin:0}</style>
